The legal texts and the data about them come from Legilux:

  Source : Legilux — Journal officiel du Grand-Duché de Luxembourg (Ministère d'État, Service central de
  législation), https://legilux.public.lu, données ouvertes https://data.legilux.public.lu.
  Copyright : Ministère d'État du Grand-Duché de Luxembourg - Service central de législation.
  Licence : Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0),
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Changes made by Lexifina: the XML of each version was converted to one Markdown file per article; struck-through
(repealed) text, notes and metadata were left out; spacing was collapsed; list numbers were printed from each list's
symbol; and the versions were arranged as git commits credited to the laws that made each change. The wording of the
law was not changed. Legilux does not endorse this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
Anyone reusing this repository as a whole must still give the Legilux attribution above, as CC BY 4.0 requires.
